pi.github.com/users/wardbell","html_url":"https://github.com/wardbell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wardbell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Current behavior**\r\nCurrently there is no visual doohickey telling user that after they clicked on a link in the sidenav the content in the document viewer is stale and will be replaced once the new content is downloaded. This results in potentially confusing behavior for users if their network connection is slow.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nIt would be nice to see some kind of visual indication that the viewer is loading new document. Either a subtle spinner (easy) or a youtube style progress bar (trickier to do since to make it meaningful we'd have to hook it up with XMLHttpRequest progress events).\r\n\r\nIn any case, we the ux element should be subtle and not overly distracting.","closed_by":{"login":"petebacondarwin","id":15655,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15655?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petebacondarwin","html_url":"https://github.com/petebacondarwin","followers_url":"h